  "question": {
    "text": "Methylene blue, from its aqueous solution, is adsorbed on activated charcoal at 25<sup>o</sup><sup>&nbsp;</sup>C. For this process, the correct statement is&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "XRjx1",
      "text": "The adsorption requires activation at 25<sup>o</sup>C.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "qh8uJ",
      "text": "The adsorption is accompanied by a decrease in enthalpy",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "f1cwR",
      "text": "The adsorption increases with increase of temperature.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NpD82",
      "text": "The adsorption is irreversible.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>It is the process of Physical adsorption as charcoal is already activated.<br />Since physical adsorption is spontaneous&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mtext>G</mtext> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;is -ve<br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mtext>G</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mtext>H</mtext> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>T</mtext> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mtext>S</mtext> </mrow> </math><br />as <math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mtext>S</mtext> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;is -ve (passage of methylene&nbsp;blue from aqueous phase over the surface of adsorbent) i.e. <math> <mrow> <mo>&#916;</mo> <mtext>H</mtext> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;is highly -ve since process is exothermic in nature.</p><p>Physical adsorption is reversible in nature.</p><p>Physical adsorption decreases with increase in temperature.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
